  "id": "allachesthesia",
  "term": "allachesthesia",
  "definition": "Allachesthesia is a neurological disorder in which a sensory input, most often touch, is felt as if it occurred at a different body location than where it was actually applied. Less commonly, this mislocalization can involve other senses as well.",
